API-11: read and write swmm_MINSLOPE in percent and apply it to the conduits

[OPTIONS] MIN_SLOPE is a percent and project.c stores MinSlope as a
fraction. getSystemValue() returned the fraction (0.005 for MIN_SLOPE 0.5),
while setSystemValue() checked the percent range 0..100 and stored the value
as given (0.5 became a 50 % slope). The minimum is applied in
conduit_getSlope() during swmm_open(), so a value set before swmm_start()
did not reach the conduits either.

Return MinSlope * 100, store value / 100, and recompute every conduit's
slope with link_updateSlope() (added by API-10) after a change.

Requires: API-10

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after API-10_swmm530.patch:
    git apply API-11_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c b/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
index a011827..44a41df 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
@@ -2952,7 +2952,7 @@ double getSystemValue(int property)
     case swmm_MINSURFAREA:
         return MinSurfArea * UCF(LENGTH) * UCF(LENGTH);
     case swmm_MINSLOPE:
-        return MinSlope;
+        return MinSlope * 100.0;
     case swmm_RUNOFFERROR:
         return RunoffError;
     case swmm_FLOWERROR:
@@ -3442,7 +3442,15 @@ static int setSystemValue(int property, double value)
     case swmm_MINSLOPE:
         if (value >= 0 && value < 100)
         {
-            MinSlope = value;
+            int j;
+
+            // --- value is a percent, as in [OPTIONS]; update the conduit
+            //     slopes computed with the old value at swmm_open
+            MinSlope = value / 100.0;
+            for (j = 0; j < Nobjects[LINK]; j++)
+            {
+                if (Link[j].type == CONDUIT) link_updateSlope(j);
+            }
             return 0;
         }
         else
